'''Bdelloida''' (de-loi′dä̤), ''n.'' [NL., < Gr. βδέλλα, a leech, + ''-oida''.] A family of rotifers that swim and creep like a leech, with the foot retractile, jointed, telescopic, and forked at the end.

'''bdellometer''' (de-lom′e-tėr), ''n.'' [< Gr. βδέλλα, a leech (< βδάλλειν, milk, suck), + μέτρον, a measure.] An instrument used as a substitute for the leech. {{smaller|It consists of a cupping-glass, to which a scarificator and an exhausting syringe are attached. ''Dunglison.''}}

